cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AxonOS RFCs"
message: >-
  If you reference or build against this component of the AxonOS
  project, please cite it using the metadata below. The canonical
  specification is the axonos-standard repository.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Denis
    family-names: Yermakou
    email: "connect@axonos.org"
    affiliation: "The AxonOS Project"
    website: "https://axonos.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AxonOS-org/axonos-rfcs"
url: "https://axonos.org"
abstract: >-
  Proposals, design documents, and architectural decision records for the AxonOS project. RFCs become normative once finalised and are tracked against the canonical standard.
keywords:
  - brain-computer interface
  - real-time systems
  - operating system
  - neurotechnology
  - rust
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0

# The version of the RFC series, not of any single RFC.
#
# This file existed without one. A citation file's entire purpose is to say
# which version somebody is citing, and this one named a repository and a
# title and left the question it exists to answer unanswered — so anyone
# citing it cited "the RFCs", which is not a thing that can be checked later.
#
# Bumped when an RFC changes status or a normative requirement changes, not
# when a typo is fixed.
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-11"
license: "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
